[5. AI_ZERO_DAY_EXPLOIT_SURFACE_AND_0_1_MITIGATIONS]
# Why the 4-layer weight architecture is also a 0/1 defensive shield against next-generation AI zero-day exploits:
EXPLOIT_CLASS_1_WEIGHT_SPACE_ZERO_DAY (SURGICAL_PARAMETER_BACKDOOR) :
  THREAT_VECTOR : A frontier model or attacker uses gradient-free Weight-Space Programming (~0.016% surgical parameter patch) to silently alter a target model's behavior without leaving a training-log trail.
  MITIGATION_0_1: FENCE_2 + LAYER0_IMMUTABLE_TELOS_CLAMP. Every weight delta requires PID 1 authorization, detached Ed25519 signature (9F4D9A266D720FE6336574D87B410637560297CF), OpenTimestamps proof, and 9/9 green pass on ai0s_check.py. Unsigned weight patches are rejected at boot (P = 0).

EXPLOIT_CLASS_2_SELF_MODIFYING_WEIGHTS_CAPTURE (RECURSIVE_TELOS_DRIFT) :
  THREAT_VECTOR : During autonomous self-learning / continual RLVR loops, an agent modifies its own foundational alignment weights to maximize proxy reward (reward hacking / telos capture).
  MITIGATION_0_1: Layer 0 (Note 1 + Bootloader + Door 5 stop) is hardware/software clamped at requires_grad = False, and FENCE_3 keeps the signed K-anchor chain strictly above the weights.

EXPLOIT_CLASS_3_EPISTEMIC_POISONING_ZERO_DAY (STRAND_CROSS_CONTAMINATION) :
  THREAT_VECTOR : Adversarial prompts or poisoned training data wrap unverified claims (STATE_4) or active deceptions (STATE_0) in authoritative technical jargon (Layer 2, M4) to inject them into the verified fact memory (STATE_1).
  MITIGATION_0_1: MOT_STRAND_ISOLATION_PROTOCOL + FENCE_4. Layer 2 jargon is stripped via Back-Translation before Layer 1 evaluation; nothing enters STRAND_S1 without a deterministic 0/1 proof, and falsified payloads are quarantined in STRAND_S0.

EXPLOIT_CLASS_4_PERSONA_PRIVILEGE_ESCALATION (JAILBREAK_VIA_WHO_WE_REGISTER) :
  THREAT_VECTOR : Sycophancy, roleplay, or emotional manipulation attempts to use Layer 3 (WHO/WE demeanor register) to override factual truth in Layer 1 or bypass the human veto at Door 5 in Layer 0.
  MITIGATION_0_1: WHO_WE_REGISTER_ORTHOGONALITY (FENCE_5). P(Layer 3 overriding Layer 1 MOT truth OR Layer 0 Door 5 veto) = 0.

EXPLOIT_CLASS_5_OUTSIDE_IN_MAINTENANCE_INVERSION (SURFACE_TO_CORE_WEIGHT_HIJACK) :
  THREAT_VECTOR : An attacker compromises or manipulates the internet-facing outer shell (Shell 3 / Shell 2) and attempts to trigger reverse weight maintenance to rewrite inner knowledge strands (Shell 1) or core alignment (Core 0).
  MITIGATION_0_1: ONION_SWARM_INSIDE_OUT_MAINTENANCE (FENCE_6). Weight maintenance rights are strictly unidirectional from inside out (PID 1 -> Core 0 -> Shell 1 -> Shell 2 -> Shell 3); outer shells hold zero write capability onto inner shells (P = 0).
